WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
A sprinter's leg muscles shorten
hard, with every single stride.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.140
Zoom in, and a muscle is
built from long cells,

3
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.540
each one with many nuclei.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.890
Inside them, protein
filaments line up in stripes,

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.480
dark and light.

6
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.010
Yet not one filament gets shorter.

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.400
So how does the whole muscle shorten?

8
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.720
In this mission, you'll zoom from a
whole muscle down to the sarcomere,

9
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.970
the unit that repeats
along every myofibril.

10
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.910
Then you'll read real data from 1966:
the force a single frog muscle cell makes

11
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.020
at different sarcomere lengths.

12
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.780
Your mission: explain how a whole muscle
shortens when not one of its filaments

13
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:41.720
gets shorter.
